 Routing changes and cluster-head retraining are deliberately out of scope.
 
+## Publication-extension ablations and all-cluster deployment
+
+A new publication-evidence pipeline now evaluates the controller
+simultaneously in every active scheduled cluster, tracks FND/HND/LND with
+censoring, measures inference latency, and compares greedy budget projection
+with an exact dynamic-programming optimum. It also defines five matched
+retraining arms across three optimizer initializations: full, no CH context,
+no trajectory-order loss, no concavity loss, and no auxiliary losses.
+
+All smoke checks pass. A five-run development pilot shows that the earlier
+one-cluster 20-node advantage does not automatically transfer to network-wide
+deployment. Under high traffic, however, HTA-MAC improves both delivery and
+packets/J over energy-proportional and online primal-dual control while reaching
+FND earlier. The 15-lineage matched retraining matrix has since completed in
+72.04 minutes at high CPU utilization, but no lineage passed the predeclared
+training gate; four lineages collapsed to all-sleep and all 15 failed reward
+convergence. The separate 20-run evaluation cohort therefore remains sealed
+pending a development-only initialization and QoS-controller repair.
+
+A literature-grounded secondary robustness hypothesis is also frozen before
+opening the final cohort: load-robust fair-energy retention (LRFER) measures the
+paired fraction of Jain-weighted packets/J retained from the reference to the
+high-traffic scenario. On the five-seed development pilot, HTA-MAC ranks first
+at 0.9561, versus 0.9274 for online primal-dual and 0.8609 for
+energy-proportional. This is explicitly exploratory, does not erase the
+20-node or FND losses, and cannot be confirmed until training gates pass and
+the sealed evaluation is run.
+
+See
+[`HTA_MAC_PUBLICATION_ABLATION_AND_ALL_CLUSTER_PILOT_20260817.md`](HTA_MAC_PUBLICATION_ABLATION_AND_ALL_CLUSTER_PILOT_20260817.md)
+for the implementation, pilot results, limitations, and required next run.
+The metric rationale and equations are in
+[`HTA_MAC_LOAD_ROBUST_FAIR_ENERGY_METRIC_20260817.md`](HTA_MAC_LOAD_ROBUST_FAIR_ENERGY_METRIC_20260817.md).
+
